\par
All SM production modes have been produced individually to estimate the dependence of the measurements on underlying assumptions of 
Higgs boson production mechanism. We have also simulated a wide range of samples that provide descriptions for exotic Higgs-like resonances productions and 
their decay to the four-lepton final state to estimate the dependence of the measurements on the Higgs boson properties. These include spin-zero, spin-one
and spin-two resonances with anomalous interactions with a pair of neutral gauge bosons ($ZZ$, $Z\gamma^{*}$, $\gamma^{*}\gamma^{*}$) described by
higher-order operators, as discussed in details in Ref.~\cite{Khachatryan:2014kca}. The details of the method used to asses the model dependence will be
described in Section ~\ref{sec:Systematics}. All these MC samples are produced using the {\sc powheg} 
generator for the representation of NLO QCD effects in the production mechanisms, and {\sc JHUgen}~\cite{Gao:2010qx,Bolognesi:2012mm,Anderson:2013afp} to 
represent the decay of these exotic resonances to four-leptons containing all spin correlations.
